{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>The stork.</b> It is the one that appears at fixed times in the year. Some say that it bestows kindness along a distant path." "<b>The heron.</b> That it will commit adultery quickly [as a wordplay on the root]." "<b>The hoopoe.</b> The Sadducees said that it is the hen. These are the fools of the world, for who told them?" "<b>The bat.</b> A small bird that flies at night. And it is a quadratic word (i.e., four-letter)." "Know that the word תשקצו with regard to birds — in grammatical analysis it is somewhat far from the word אל תשקצו את נפשותיכם, for נפשותיכם is the object, but with regard to a bird its sense is that you should know that they are detestable, and they shall be considered by you as detestable. And every small swarming creature that flies from time to time and goes on four [legs] is detestable."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:30.526180331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}